the problem is with the ldr (load register) instraction from the address aav.aav.0x000113b0 
the name should not be an auto address value

    -then i runed :
        $ meson test -C build | tee before_fix.log
    this command logs the test on the rizin in the file before_fix.log

ROOT causer of the issue :
    When multiple flags exist at the same offset, auto-generated aav flags could be preferred over more meaningful symbol/import names.
        Also, operand-string rendering did not fully apply the same dereference hop logic already used in comment resolution.
how i addressed the issue:
my fix provide :
        Updated preferred flag resolution in flag.c:439-465:
        Detect auto aav flags.
        Prefer a non-aav fallback when available at the same address.
        Added operand post-processing in disasm.c:885-955:
        Detect aav.aav.0x... patterns.
        Dereference using analysis refptr width.
        Resolve and substitute with a better non-aav symbol when found.
        Hooked this resolver in op-string build flow in disasm.c:1132.
-after fix :
    $ meson compile -C build
then
    - i test with valgrind to check for a leak or a memory miss usage
    - i performed the same test provided by the issue 
